  "dg.net.cap": "The small network from chapter 7 (d = {d}). Solid lines are the forward pass that computes probabilities; dashed lines are the parameters being nudged backward during training. The three blocks E, W and b hold {total} numbers in all; a real chat model stacks dozens of attention layers and other computation between E and W.",
  "dg.net.in": "Previous token, e.g. “{t}”",
